WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:26.693 --> 00:00:28.561
It's like reading my mind.

00:00:28.561 --> 00:00:29.896
It's magic.

00:00:33.266 --> 00:00:34.501
We're innovating

00:00:34.501 --> 00:00:36.569
at a scale like never before.

00:00:37.037 --> 00:00:38.905
It takes what you prompt it with

00:00:38.905 --> 00:00:40.507
and just runs with it.

00:00:45.111 --> 00:00:46.146
Everything is linked.

00:00:46.146 --> 00:00:47.847
Everything is easy to use.

00:00:48.815 --> 00:00:51.117
We're accelerating how fast we can deliver

00:00:51.117 --> 00:00:53.053
solutions to our fans, to our business.

00:00:55.488 --> 00:00:57.123
It takes the hands-on time

00:00:57.123 --> 00:00:58.291
that the provider has to spend

00:00:58.291 --> 00:00:59.292
with the computer

00:00:59.292 --> 00:01:02.195
and puts that time back with the patient.

00:01:02.195 --> 00:01:04.831
It allows for the patient and doctor

00:01:04.831 --> 00:01:06.699
to be a patient and a doctor

00:01:06.699 --> 00:01:08.068
like it used to be.

00:01:08.068 --> 00:01:08.902
It's fundamentally

00:01:08.902 --> 00:01:10.070
about amplifying what
every person is able to do.

00:01:10.070 --> 00:01:11.271
every person is able to do.

00:01:14.874 --> 00:01:17.043
This opens up the opportunity

00:01:17.043 --> 00:01:17.877
for that farmer,

00:01:17.877 --> 00:01:18.978
for that girl in the village

00:01:18.978 --> 00:01:20.580
who's trying to go to college

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:21.948
to find out what more

00:01:21.948 --> 00:01:22.782
can they do with their life.

00:01:56.900 --> 00:02:02.355
Good morning.

00:02:02.355 --> 00:02:02.956
Good morning.

00:02:02.956 --> 00:02:04.908
It's fantastic to see you all.

00:02:04.908 --> 00:02:06.910
Welcome to Build, all of those

00:02:06.910 --> 00:02:08.178
who made it here.

00:02:08.178 --> 00:02:08.661
You know, it's

00:02:08.661 --> 00:02:10.513
fantastic to be back together

00:02:10.513 --> 00:02:13.333
physically and everyone joining online.

00:02:13.333 --> 00:02:16.302
You know, these developer conferences are special

00:02:16.302 --> 00:02:19.639
times, special places to be,

00:02:19.639 --> 00:02:23.927
especially when platform shifts are in the air.

00:02:23.927 --> 00:02:29.682
I distinctly remember my first PDC in 1991,

00:02:29.682 --> 00:02:33.136
driving up 101 into Moscone Center,

00:02:33.136 --> 00:02:37.240
and my life changed after that

00:02:37.240 --> 00:02:38.474
developer conference.

00:02:38.474 --> 00:02:40.243
So it's exciting to be able

00:02:40.243 --> 00:02:44.414
to come back to Build 2023 with that same sense

00:02:44.414 --> 00:02:48.401
of anticipation of something big that is shifting

00:02:48.401 --> 00:02:51.020
around us as developers.

00:02:51.020 --> 00:02:53.506
To just sort of put this in perspective,

00:02:53.506 --> 00:02:57.043
in fact, last summer I was reading

00:02:57.043 --> 00:02:59.963
Mitchell Waldrop's Dream Machine

00:02:59.963 --> 00:03:03.516
while I was playing with DV3, as GPT-4

00:03:03.516 --> 00:03:07.187
was called then, Da Vinci 3

00:03:07.187 --> 00:03:10.456
and it just brought to -

00:03:10.456 --> 00:03:14.894
it brought in perspective what this is all about.

00:03:14.894 --> 00:03:18.314
I think that that concept of “Dream Machine”

00:03:18.314 --> 00:03:21.084
perhaps best communicates

00:03:21.084 --> 00:03:23.269
what we have really been doing

00:03:23.269 --> 00:03:24.971
over the last 70 years, right?

00:03:24.971 --> 00:03:25.638
All the ways,

00:03:25.638 --> 00:03:27.190
starting with

00:03:27.190 --> 00:03:29.576
what Vannevar Bush wrote in his most

00:03:29.576 --> 00:03:31.211
seminal paper

00:03:31.211 --> 00:03:32.195
As We May Think,

00:03:32.195 --> 00:03:33.980
where he had all these concepts

00:03:33.980 --> 00:03:36.349
like associative memory,

00:03:36.349 --> 00:03:38.484
or what Licklider was the first one

00:03:38.484 --> 00:03:39.736
who even conceptualized

00:03:39.736 --> 00:03:42.472
the human computer symbiosis,

00:03:42.472 --> 00:03:44.874
The Mother of All Demos

00:03:44.874 --> 00:03:50.079
that came in ‘68 to the Xerox Alto,

00:03:50.079 --> 00:03:53.449
and then, of course, the PDC that I attended,

00:03:53.449 --> 00:03:57.887
which was the PC server one in ‘91,

00:03:57.887 --> 00:04:01.724
‘93 is when we had the mosaic moment,

00:04:01.724 --> 00:04:04.811
then there was iPhone and the cloud,

00:04:04.811 --> 00:04:08.982
and all of these would be one continuous journey.

00:04:08.982 --> 00:04:12.285
And then, in fact, the other thing I always loved

00:04:12.285 --> 00:04:13.219
is Jobs's

00:04:13.219 --> 00:04:14.954
description of computers

00:04:14.954 --> 00:04:16.606
as bicycles for the mind.

00:04:16.606 --> 00:04:18.258
It's sort of a beautiful metaphor.

00:04:18.258 --> 00:04:19.092
I think it captures

00:04:19.092 --> 00:04:22.161
the essence of what computing is.

00:04:22.161 --> 00:04:24.864
But then last November,

00:04:24.864 --> 00:04:27.100
we got an upgrade, right?

00:04:27.100 --> 00:04:32.171
We went from the bicycle to the steam engine.

00:04:32.171 --> 00:04:35.275
With the launch of ChatGPT,

00:04:35.275 --> 00:04:39.679
it was like the mosaic moment for this generation

00:04:39.679 --> 00:04:42.015
of the AI platform.

00:04:42.015 --> 00:04:45.685
And now we look forward to, as developers,

00:04:45.685 --> 00:04:48.404
what we can do going forward.

00:04:48.404 --> 00:04:50.473
And so it's an exciting time.

00:04:50.473 --> 00:04:53.393
And in fact, every layer of the software stack

00:04:53.393 --> 00:04:56.629
is going to be changed forever.

00:04:56.629 --> 00:04:58.848
And no better place to start

00:04:58.848 --> 00:05:01.851
than the actual developer stack, right?

00:05:01.884 --> 00:05:03.886
We, as developers,

00:05:03.886 --> 00:05:07.790
how do we build is fundamentally changing.

00:05:07.790 --> 00:05:10.960
In fact, when I think about how we build,

00:05:10.960 --> 00:05:13.997
I think about first Codespaces, right?

00:05:13.997 --> 00:05:17.233
Being able to set up that environment in,

00:05:17.233 --> 00:05:19.902
you know, in seconds was versus minutes.

00:05:19.902 --> 00:05:21.821
Dev Box, you know,

00:05:21.821 --> 00:05:23.423
instead of waiting for a day

00:05:23.423 --> 00:05:24.173
for your managed

00:05:24.173 --> 00:05:25.541
dev box to be set up,

00:05:25.541 --> 00:05:28.277
you have it in less than an hour.

00:05:28.277 --> 00:05:31.514
If you think about Copilot, what it does to you,

00:05:31.514 --> 00:05:32.815
and Copilot X,

00:05:32.815 --> 00:05:34.784
in terms of driving the overall flow

00:05:34.784 --> 00:05:39.072
and productivity, which is, what, 54% or so up.

00:05:39.072 --> 00:05:40.823
And then of course GitHub Actions

00:05:40.823 --> 00:05:43.993
and Azure Deployment Environments,

00:05:43.993 --> 00:05:46.913
really making that possible for you to stay.

00:05:46.913 --> 00:05:48.498
In fact, one of the things that I keep on

00:05:48.498 --> 00:05:50.450
bugging Scott Guthrie for years is,

00:05:50.450 --> 00:05:52.285
“Hey, I want to stay in VS code,

00:05:52.285 --> 00:05:53.953
I want to stay in command line

00:05:53.953 --> 00:05:56.089
and let me do everything there.”

00:05:56.089 --> 00:05:59.142
We are close, close to that dream.

00:05:59.142 --> 00:06:02.628
And that to me is bringing back

00:06:02.628 --> 00:06:05.365
both the joy of programming

00:06:05.365 --> 00:06:08.201
and the flow of programming.

00:06:08.201 --> 00:06:10.603
That ability to be able to stay on

00:06:10.603 --> 00:06:14.090
task, it's just so wonderful to see.

00:06:14.090 --> 00:06:19.195
So how we build software is radically different,

00:06:19.195 --> 00:06:23.332
but what we are going to build as developers

00:06:23.332 --> 00:06:27.370
is really the story of this developer conference.

00:06:27.370 --> 00:06:28.971
And what we build -

00:06:28.971 --> 00:06:30.173
we've been, you know,

00:06:30.173 --> 00:06:33.042
it's not like I came in on January 1st and said,

00:06:33.042 --> 00:06:34.577
“Let's start doing press releases.”

00:06:34.577 --> 00:06:37.063
But it does feel like that.

00:06:37.063 --> 00:06:39.348
It does feel like every week

00:06:39.348 --> 00:06:41.617
there is something new and,

00:06:41.617 --> 00:06:43.786
you know, we’re infusing

00:06:43.786 --> 00:06:47.440
this new AI stack across all layers of it, right?

00:06:47.440 --> 00:06:50.626
So we started with tooling in GitHub -

00:06:50.626 --> 00:06:53.513
or rather, Copilot in GitHub.

00:06:53.513 --> 00:06:56.783
We did Copilot in Power Platform.

00:06:56.783 --> 00:06:58.151
And when it comes to productivity,

00:06:58.151 --> 00:07:00.203
Copilot in Microsoft 365,

00:07:00.203 --> 00:07:01.404
Copilot in Viva.

00:07:01.404 --> 00:07:02.605
With business process, it's

00:07:02.605 --> 00:07:05.425
the copilot in Dynamics 365.

00:07:05.425 --> 00:07:09.412
And when it comes to industry sort of workflows,

00:07:09.412 --> 00:07:11.147
what Nuance has done with DAX

00:07:11.147 --> 00:07:14.000
or the Security Copilot.

00:07:14.000 --> 00:07:15.051
Or the copilot,

00:07:15.051 --> 00:07:17.620
of course, for the web in Bing and Edge,

00:07:17.620 --> 00:07:20.506
features in LinkedIn, which are driven by AI,

00:07:20.506 --> 00:07:22.525
and of course the AI infrastructure

00:07:22.525 --> 00:07:24.627
with Azure OpenAI APIs

00:07:24.627 --> 00:07:26.562
and everything else around it, right?

00:07:26.562 --> 00:07:28.731
So every layer of the stack

00:07:28.731 --> 00:07:31.934
is profoundly changing.

00:07:31.934 --> 00:07:35.238
And we today are going to -

00:07:35.238 --> 00:07:36.856
as part of this developer conference,

00:07:36.856 --> 00:07:40.960
we're going to have 50+ more announcements,

00:07:40.960 --> 00:07:44.147
but I want to highlight five of them.

00:07:44.147 --> 00:07:48.084
The first is we are bringing

00:07:48.084 --> 00:07:51.888
search grounding in Bing to ChatGPT.

00:07:51.888 --> 00:07:53.873
We are very excited about this.

00:07:53.873 --> 00:08:00.313
Yeah, you can clap!

00:08:00.313 --> 00:08:04.183
Look, ChatGPT is the most fast-growing

00:08:04.183 --> 00:08:07.670
consumer app we've ever seen

00:08:07.670 --> 00:08:11.090
and such grounding is a very key feature, right?

00:08:11.090 --> 00:08:13.092
So that all the information is current

00:08:13.092 --> 00:08:15.811
and grounded by what you have

00:08:15.811 --> 00:08:17.480
from the crawl and the index.

00:08:17.480 --> 00:08:18.798
And so it's fantastic to see

00:08:18.798 --> 00:08:20.016
that we are excited to be able -

00:08:20.016 --> 00:08:22.318
it’s going to launch in ChatGPT+

00:08:22.318 --> 00:08:23.519
immediately and quickly coming

00:08:23.519 --> 00:08:25.121
even to the free tier.

00:08:25.121 --> 00:08:28.524
And this is just the start of what we plan to do

00:08:28.524 --> 00:08:30.059
with our partners in OpenAI

00:08:30.059 --> 00:08:35.364
to bring the best of Bing to the ChatGPT experience.

00:08:35.364 --> 00:08:37.149
Next, we are bringing

00:08:37.149 --> 00:08:40.269
the copilot to the biggest canvas of all:

00:08:40.269 --> 00:08:47.260
Windows.

00:08:47.260 --> 00:08:49.245
You're going to hear a lot from Panos

00:08:49.245 --> 00:08:52.248
tomorrow about it, but I think that this is going

00:08:52.248 --> 00:08:55.651
to make every user a power user of Windows.

00:08:55.651 --> 00:08:58.654
Let's roll the video.

00:10:22.004 --> 00:10:25.007
It's so cool.

00:10:29.745 --> 00:10:32.632
So we're going to talk a lot more about Windows,

00:10:32.632 --> 00:10:36.319
you know, tomorrow when Panos is up here.

00:10:36.319 --> 00:10:39.522
The other thing that we're also very excited to

00:10:39.522 --> 00:10:42.892
launch is the Copilot stack, right?

00:10:42.892 --> 00:10:44.694
After all, we've built all these copilots

00:10:44.694 --> 00:10:47.296
with one common architectural stack.

00:10:47.296 --> 00:10:48.731
We want to make that available

00:10:48.731 --> 00:10:50.082
so that everyone here

00:10:50.082 --> 00:10:51.767
can build their own copilot

00:10:51.767 --> 00:10:53.719
for their applications.

00:10:53.719 --> 00:10:56.889
We will have everything from the AI

00:10:56.889 --> 00:11:00.309
infrastructure to the foundation models to the

00:11:00.309 --> 00:11:03.529
AI orchestration all the way up to your copilot

00:11:03.529 --> 00:11:04.947
and its extensibility.

00:11:04.947 --> 00:11:06.916
In fact, the other thing that we're going to do

00:11:06.916 --> 00:11:07.933
is have common

00:11:07.933 --> 00:11:10.219
extensibility across

00:11:10.219 --> 00:11:11.837
all of these surfaces, right?

00:11:11.837 --> 00:11:13.422
Whether it is ChatGPT,

00:11:13.422 --> 00:11:16.492
Bing Chat, Microsoft 365 Copilot,

00:11:16.492 --> 00:11:18.160
or all of the Microsoft copilots,

00:11:18.160 --> 00:11:20.296
and of course, your own copilots,

00:11:20.296 --> 00:11:23.382
we can share the same extensibility model.

00:11:23.382 --> 00:11:25.217
This is one of the most powerful things

00:11:25.217 --> 00:11:26.652
for your developers -

00:11:26.652 --> 00:11:29.004
for every developer to be able to write a plugin

00:11:29.004 --> 00:11:31.757
and have it reach billions of users

00:11:31.757 --> 00:11:33.793
across all of these surface areas.

00:11:33.793 --> 00:11:36.228
So to be able to show you everything

00:11:36.228 --> 00:11:37.012
in action

00:11:37.012 --> 00:11:39.582
from both the plugin extensibility

00:11:39.582 --> 00:11:41.684
to all of the copilots we announced,

00:11:41.684 --> 00:11:44.303
let me right up on stage Yusuf Mehdi

00:11:44.303 --> 00:11:45.521
to come show you all of this.

00:11:45.521 --> 00:11:48.641
Yusuf, let me throw it over to you.

00:11:48.641 --> 00:11:52.344
Hi, everybody.

00:11:52.344 --> 00:11:53.879
We're making fast progress on

00:11:53.879 --> 00:11:56.065
delivering our vision of your copilot

00:11:56.065 --> 00:11:58.134
for the web and for business.

00:11:58.134 --> 00:11:59.585
And today, as Satya said,

00:11:59.585 --> 00:12:01.120
we're excited to announce

00:12:01.120 --> 00:12:01.670
that we're going to bring

00:12:01.670 --> 00:12:03.989
ChatGPT and Bing together

00:12:03.989 --> 00:12:06.208
as the default search experience

00:12:06.208 --> 00:12:07.877
to give you higher quality answers

00:12:07.877 --> 00:12:09.462
and more timely answers.

00:12:09.462 --> 00:12:10.830
Let's take a look.

00:12:10.830 --> 00:12:12.381
Here I am in ChatGPT.

00:12:12.381 --> 00:12:13.933
And as you can see now,

00:12:13.933 --> 00:12:15.234
Bing is the default

00:12:15.234 --> 00:12:16.919
and when I come in and select it,

00:12:16.919 --> 00:12:19.321
I can now ask sort of real-time queries.

00:12:19.321 --> 00:12:20.206
For example,

00:12:20.206 --> 00:12:22.708
let's ask what I should expect to hear

00:12:22.708 --> 00:12:24.894
about Build and .NET.

00:12:24.894 --> 00:12:26.695
And what you can see is the results

00:12:26.695 --> 00:12:28.247
now are more up to date.

00:12:28.247 --> 00:12:29.598
They include fresh content

00:12:29.598 --> 00:12:31.167
and they include citations.

00:12:31.167 --> 00:12:32.418
In fact, if you can see the links

00:12:32.418 --> 00:12:33.569
on that page there,

00:12:33.569 --> 00:12:34.403
you can click those

00:12:34.403 --> 00:12:35.538
and those will take you straight

00:12:35.538 --> 00:12:38.491
to a web page that's sourced by Bing.

00:12:38.491 --> 00:12:39.542
We're also excited -

00:12:39.542 --> 00:12:40.943
yeah, absolutely, you can clap!

00:12:45.064 --> 00:12:46.549
We're also excited to announce

00:12:46.549 --> 00:12:47.366
that we're going to bring

00:12:47.383 --> 00:12:50.936
interoperability between ChatGPT and Bing

00:12:50.936 --> 00:12:51.821
for plugins.

00:12:51.821 --> 00:12:53.005
So you write them once

00:12:53.005 --> 00:12:54.673
and they're going to run everywhere.

00:12:54.673 --> 00:12:56.709
So as you can see here in ChatGPT,

00:12:56.709 --> 00:12:58.844
I've got Zillow and Instacart enabled,

00:12:58.844 --> 00:13:00.162
but I want to show them to you

00:13:00.162 --> 00:13:01.130
here in Bing Chat.

00:13:01.130 --> 00:13:02.531
So we'll flip over

00:13:02.531 --> 00:13:03.549
and you can see again,

00:13:03.549 --> 00:13:05.384
I've got the same plugins now

00:13:05.384 --> 00:13:08.154
in both Bing Chat and in ChatGPT.

00:13:08.154 --> 00:13:09.889
And what we're going to show you now is

00:13:09.889 --> 00:13:11.106
I'll do a search here for

00:13:11.106 --> 00:13:12.525
houses in Chicago.

00:13:12.525 --> 00:13:13.959
And I can ask for a set of criteria,

00:13:13.959 --> 00:13:14.743
I'll learn a little bit about

00:13:14.743 --> 00:13:16.061
the neighborhoods.

00:13:16.061 --> 00:13:18.531
And now I can automatically call Zillow

00:13:18.531 --> 00:13:19.165
by saying,

00:13:19.165 --> 00:13:20.416
hey, give me three houses

00:13:20.416 --> 00:13:21.801
in a certain price range

00:13:21.801 --> 00:13:23.619
that meet my criteria.

00:13:23.619 --> 00:13:25.137
And what you can see

00:13:25.137 --> 00:13:27.106
is now I get these great options

00:13:27.106 --> 00:13:28.007
and I'm also going to get

00:13:28.007 --> 00:13:29.024
all of the other great things

00:13:29.024 --> 00:13:30.009
you get with Bing, like

00:13:30.009 --> 00:13:33.512
helpful city guides and maps and prompts.

00:13:33.512 --> 00:13:34.330
I'm going to tell you now how

00:13:34.330 --> 00:13:35.331
we're going to further add value

00:13:35.331 --> 00:13:36.699
to the plugins that you write.

00:13:36.699 --> 00:13:37.299
They're going to work

00:13:37.299 --> 00:13:39.385
not just in chat and ChatGPT,

00:13:39.385 --> 00:13:39.885
they're going to work

00:13:39.885 --> 00:13:41.620
across the entire Web,

00:13:41.620 --> 00:13:43.489
courtesy of the Edge browser.

00:13:43.489 --> 00:13:44.456
So here's an example.

00:13:44.456 --> 00:13:45.374
I'm on a web page

00:13:45.374 --> 00:13:47.593
here checking out a recipe for a cake,

00:13:47.593 --> 00:13:49.645
and now I can call Bing Chat

00:13:49.645 --> 00:13:50.746
and ask it to tell me,

00:13:50.746 --> 00:13:52.031
hey, give me the ingredients

00:13:52.031 --> 00:13:53.299
from this web page.

00:13:53.299 --> 00:13:54.567
And notice Bing can read

00:13:54.567 --> 00:13:56.001
the context of the Web page,

00:13:56.001 --> 00:13:57.703
understand those ingredients,

00:13:57.703 --> 00:13:58.938
put them into chat,

00:13:58.938 --> 00:13:59.839
and then I can say,

00:13:59.839 --> 00:14:01.457
hey, give me a shopping list for this,

00:14:01.457 --> 00:14:02.658
and it'll automatically call

00:14:02.658 --> 00:14:04.343
the Instacart plugin,

00:14:04.343 --> 00:14:05.561
take those ingredients

00:14:05.561 --> 00:14:06.345
right off the page,

00:14:06.345 --> 00:14:09.114
and put them into an Instacart shopping.

00:14:09.114 --> 00:14:10.249
And with one click,

00:14:10.249 --> 00:14:11.200
I can get those now

